[center][size=5][b]No Auto-Greet[/b][/size]
[size=3]Traders stop calling out to you as you walk past. Everyone else stays vanilla.[/size][/center]

[center][url=https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e77fdfd91d2b39292acf37e031a67d417fbe8a4b4509a2743029ef6b950ee39b][img]https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2FReidenXerx%2Ffo4-no-auto-greet%2Fmaster%2Fdocs%2Fvt-badge.json&style=for-the-badge&labelColor=2b2b2b&logo=virustotal&logoColor=white[/img][/url] [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-no-auto-greet/blob/master/LICENSE][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue?style=for-the-badge&labelColor=2b2b2b[/img][/url] [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-no-auto-greet][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/source-GitHub-181717?style=for-the-badge&labelColor=2b2b2b&logo=github&logoColor=white[/img][/url]
[img]https://img.shields.io/badge/Fallout%204-1.10.163%20%C2%B7%201.11%20AE-4a4a4a?style=for-the-badge&labelColor=2b2b2b[/img] [url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/requires-F4SE-8a5a00?style=for-the-badge&labelColor=2b2b2b[/img][/url] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/requires-Runtime%20Database-8a5a00?style=for-the-badge&labelColor=2b2b2b[/img][/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-no-auto-greet@73b07f9be7a49378921aeb3a9a963c12d0249831/docs/img/card.jpg[/img][/center]

In the vanilla game, a trader opens a conversation, camera and all, or calls out a hello the moment you walk by. This mod stops that. Traders wait until you press Talk, and then everything they have to say still plays.

[size=5][b]In short[/b][/size]

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Traders no longer open a conversation or call out to you on their own.[/*]
[*]Press Talk and they say everything they normally would.[/*]
[*]Companions, settlers, guards and everyone else keep greeting you as they always did.[/*]
[/list][b]What you need[/b]: [url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/]F4SE[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url].
[b]How it goes[/b]: install with Vortex or MO2. See [b]Install[/b], below.

[size=4][b]Who counts as a trader[/b][/size]

Anyone in a faction that has a merchant container, the same faction the game opens bartering from: 108 factions in the vanilla game and DLC, including the settlement shop factions (armor, clinic, clothing, weapons, bar, misc). That covers Diamond City's and Goodneighbor's shopkeepers (Myrna, Arturo, Percy, Takahashi, Kleo), the doctors, the traveling merchants, and the Far Harbor and Nuka-World traders. Other mods' traders count too. Anyone who is or has been your companion is left alone.

[size=4][b]How it works[/b][/size]

The game has one function that decides whether an NPC greets you on their own, and the plugin skips it for traders. It is the same function in 1.10.163 and the Anniversary Edition 1.11.240. Greetings that a quest forces take a separate path and are untouched, and Talk works as always. The log is [font=Courier New]Documents\My Games\Fallout4\F4SE\NoAutoGreet.log[/font].

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]

Install with Vortex or MO2: the installer checks your setup first. Installing by hand is not supported. There is no plugin file, so nothing takes a load-order slot. Needs [url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/]F4SE[/url] (0.6.23 on 1.10.163, 0.7.9 on the Anniversary Edition) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url] on both.

[size=4][b]Incompatibilities[/b][/size]

None known. A trader's own story moment (the Vault 88 Overseer, for example) now waits for you to press Talk.

Source and licence (MIT): [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-no-auto-greet]github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-no-auto-greet[/url].
